## T6.1 — Budget enforcement primitives (`max_children` / `max_depth`)
- **Files:** `crates/harness-core/src/budget.rs` (only)
- **Description:** Extend the existing `BudgetCheck` trait with two new methods and back them with new `BudgetError` variants, keeping the file's existing style:

```rust
// budget.rs — additions only, existing check_usage/check_cost untouched

#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error, PartialEq, Eq, Clone)]
pub enum BudgetError {
    #[error("token/cost budget exceeded: {0}")]
    Exceeded(String),
    #[error("cost budget exceeded")]
    CostExceeded,
    #[error("max_children ({limit}) exceeded: already have {current}")]
    TooManyChildren { limit: u32, current: u32 },
    #[error("max_depth ({limit}) exceeded: current depth is {current}")]
    MaxDepthExceeded { limit: u32, current: u32 },
}

pub trait BudgetCheck {
    fn check_usage(&self, usage: &ModelUsage) -> Result<(), BudgetError>;
    fn check_cost(&self, cost: &Cost) -> Result<(), BudgetError>;
    fn check_children(&self, current_children: u32) -> Result<(), BudgetError>;
    fn check_depth(&self, current_depth: u32) -> Result<(), BudgetError>;
}

impl BudgetCheck for AgentBudget {
    // ...existing bodies unchanged...

    fn check_children(&self, current_children: u32) -> Result<(), BudgetError> {
        if let Some(limit) = self.max_children {
            if current_children >= limit {
                return Err(BudgetError::TooManyChildren { limit, current: current_children });
            }
        }
        Ok(())
    }

    fn check_depth(&self, current_depth: u32) -> Result<(), BudgetError> {
        if let Some(limit) = self.max_depth {
            if current_depth >= limit {
                return Err(BudgetError::MaxDepthExceeded { limit, current: current_depth });
            }
        }
        Ok(())
    }
}
```
- **Acceptance criteria:** unit tests in `budget.rs` (existing `#[cfg(test)]` module) covering: `check_children` passes at `current < limit`, rejects at `current == limit`; `check_depth` same; both return `Ok(())` when the corresponding `Option` is `None` (unbounded).
- **Effort:** S
- **Depends on:** none (pure addition, no callers yet)

