## T6.2 — Child capability derivation (full `AgentCapabilities`, not just toolset)
- **Files:** `crates/harness-core/src/capabilities.rs` (only)
- **Description:** Add a new method beside the existing `derive_child_capabilities` (which stays untouched/reused internally) that produces a complete child `AgentCapabilities`, enforcing `can_spawn_agents` non-escalation (a child of a non-spawning agent can never spawn) and depth capping via `max_child_depth`:

```rust
impl AgentCapabilities {
    // existing derive_child_capabilities(&self, inheritance: &ToolInheritance) -> Result<AgentToolset, CapabilityError> unchanged

    pub fn derive_child_agent_capabilities(
        &self,
        inheritance: &ToolInheritance,
        workspace_override: Option<WorkspaceCapabilities>,
        backend_override: Option<BackendCapabilities>,
    ) -> Result<AgentCapabilities, CapabilityError> {
        let tools = self.derive_child_capabilities(inheritance)?;

        let max_child_depth = match (self.max_child_depth, ) {
            (Some(d),) if d == 0 => None, // parent forbids further descent
            (Some(d),) => Some(d - 1),
            (None,) => None,
        };

        Ok(AgentCapabilities {
            tools,
            can_spawn_agents: self.can_spawn_agents && max_child_depth != Some(0),
            max_child_depth,
            workspace: workspace_override.unwrap_or_else(|| self.workspace.clone()),
            backend: backend_override.unwrap_or_else(|| self.backend.clone()),
        })
    }
}
```
- **Acceptance criteria:** unit test: parent with `can_spawn_agents: false` yields child with `can_spawn_agents: false` regardless of input; parent `max_child_depth: Some(1)` yields child `max_child_depth: Some(0)` and `can_spawn_agents: false` (grandchildren blocked); `ToolInheritance::Subset([fs.read])` from a parent with `fs.read` (delegatable) + `shell.exec` (not delegatable) yields a child toolset containing only `fs.read` (reuses existing, already-correct `derive_child_capabilities` logic — this test just confirms the wrapper doesn't regress it).
