## T6.11 — Child completion/failure usage rollup and status transition
- **Files:** `crates/harness-core/src/transitions.rs` (only)
- **Description:** Fix the two gaps identified in `child_completed`/`child_failed`: usage is discarded, and `AgentStatus::WaitingForChildren` is never resumed from. Requires a bridging function between the two `AgentUsageSummary` types (add it locally in `transitions.rs` as a private `fn bridge_usage_summary(protocol: &harness_protocol::usage::AgentUsageSummary) -> harness_core::usage::AgentUsageSummary`, since it's a pure conversion used only here):

```rust
fn child_completed(&mut self, agent_id: AgentId, result: AgentResult) -> Vec<AgentEffect> {
    self.state.children.retain(|c| *c != agent_id);
    self.usage.add_child_summary(agent_id, bridge_usage_summary(&result.usage)); // new UsageLedger method, see below
    let mut effects = vec![AgentEffect::Emit {
        event: AgentEvent::ChildAgentCompleted { agent_id, outcome: AgentOutcome::Success },
    }];
    if self.state.children.is_empty() && self.state.status == AgentStatus::WaitingForChildren {
        self.state.status = AgentStatus::Idle;
        effects.push(AgentEffect::Emit {
            event: AgentEvent::StateChanged { from: AgentStatus::WaitingForChildren, to: AgentStatus::Idle },
        });
    }
    effects
}
```
